3.5 — Confidence notes / caveats
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  1. FILE COUNT (2,707) — high confidence.
     Every leaf in the source tree has been enumerated exactly once.

  2. FOLDER COUNT (~443, expanded) — medium confidence.
     Exact number depends on how you count:
       - Java/Kotlin package expansion: java/com/sarathi/sris/X = 5 folders
       - Python subpackage expansion:   a/b/c/  = 3 folders
       - Flutter path expansion:        lib/core/config = 3 folders
       - TypeScript src/ paths:         src/data/prisma = 3 folders
     If your reference collapsed these into 1 line each, subtract roughly
     ~180 from the expanded total (~443 → ~260). Both are valid, just
     different conventions.

  3. APPROXIMATE FOLDER COUNTS for large buckets (marked with ~)
     are due to nested package expansion in:
       clients/     (many src/…/…/ paths in web and mobile)
       services/    (java/com/sarathi/sris/… in s2, s3; node src/…/… in all)
       infra/       (provisioning/, dashboards/{dev,test,prod}/, etc.)
       sris-launcher/ (java/com/sarathi/sris/launcher + python packages)

  4. DOTFILES count as files. If your reference ignores .gitkeep /
     .gitignore / .env*.example, subtract ~55 from the total
     (2,707 → ~2,652).

  5. .gitkeep files (~30) are counted as real files. If you exclude them,
     subtract ~30.

  6. Duplicated names (README.md, index.ts, package.json, etc.) are
     counted once per physical occurrence, not deduplicated.

  7. The infra/secrets/{dev,test,prod}/.gitkeep files are counted as 3
     files even though the folders are intentionally empty in the repo.

